# SPM structure

## Target layout

- `Sources/SelectBeaconSDK/Public/` — host-facing types and `SelectBeaconSDK`
- `Detection/` — ranging, windows, presence, location, permissions, lifecycle
- `Networking/` — upload coordinator, auth, payload encoder, device id
- `Persistence/` — durable queue
- `Configuration/`, `Support/` — config, clock, diagnostics, dependencies
- `Sources/SelectBeaconAppSupport/` — Select-owned adapter only; imports SPI

## Visibility

- Prefer `internal` by default; `public` only for the standard product surface
- Select-only APIs: `@_spi(SelectApp)` on the core module; apps use AppSupport
- Do not `@testable`-require production hosts; tests may use `@testable` / SPI

## Seams

- Inject clocks, queues, engines, path observers, schedulers, device id via `SDKDependencies`
- Pure logic (e.g. `ObservationWindowStore`) takes `now` as an argument
- Keep Apple types (`CLLocation`, `UIDevice`) behind thin adapters

## Package

- Products: `SelectBeaconSDK`, `SelectBeaconAppSupport`
- No new package dependencies without an explicit product decision
